# Khadas Edge1 (RK3399) - Android TV 14 fstab.
#
# Non-A/B layout with a discrete recovery partition, so no slotselect. The
# partition set is the GPT in flash/partitions.tsv, written by the generated
# flash-emmc.sh - not a Rockchip update.img, which this tree no longer produces.
#
# system/system_ext/product/vendor/odm are logical partitions inside super
# (PRODUCT_USE_DYNAMIC_PARTITIONS := true). The Android 10 fstab this replaces
# mounted them as fixed /dev/block/by-name/ devices.
#
# <src>  <mnt_point>  <type>  <mnt_flags,options>  <fs_mgr_flags>

# ---- logical partitions in super ----
#
# avb=vbmeta, not a bare avb. First-stage init builds its list of vbmeta partitions
# from the device tree's /firmware/android/vbmeta/parts or, failing that, from the
# partition named after "avb=" in this fstab (init/first_stage_mount.cpp, the
# FirstStageMountVBootV2 constructor). This board has no such DT node and a bare
# "avb" names nothing, so the list was empty and the first boot that got this far
# stopped with "Failed to read vbmeta partitions" / "Missing vbmeta partitions".
# There is one vbmeta partition and it carries every hashtree descriptor
# (BoardConfig.mk chains nothing), so all five name it.
system       /system       ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount,avb=vbmeta
system_ext   /system_ext   ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount,avb=vbmeta
product      /product      ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount,avb=vbmeta
vendor       /vendor       ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount,avb=vbmeta
odm          /odm          ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount,avb=vbmeta

# ---- metadata: required by dynamic partitions, holds the FBE keys ----
/dev/block/by-name/metadata  /metadata  ext4  noatime,nosuid,nodev,discard  wait,formattable,first_stage_mount

# ---- userdata ----
#
# File-based encryption at policy v2.
#
# This line said v1 for as long as the tree targeted the Khadas 4.19 BSP, where
# v2 needed fscrypt backports that kernel did not have. The kernel is mainline
# 6.12 now; v2 policies have been upstream since 5.4, so the reason for pinning
# v1 is gone. v1 was only ever permitted here because PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL
# is 29 - an upgrade device - and it is deprecated for anything newer.
#
# Metadata encryption (keydirectory=, dm-default-key) is still omitted. That is a
# choice, not a limitation: 6.12 has dm-default-key only in the Android common
# kernels, not upstream, so /metadata would have to be left unencrypted anyway.
#
# No "resize": Android 14's libfstab does not know it ("[libfstab] Warning: unknown
# flag: resize" on the board) and ignores it. userdata fills its partition anyway:
# it is formatted on the device, at whatever size the partition is.
/dev/block/by-name/userdata  /data  f2fs  noatime,nosuid,nodev,discard,reserve_root=32768,resgid=1065,fsync_mode=nobarrier  latemount,wait,check,fileencryption=aes-256-xts:aes-256-cts:v2,quota,formattable

# ---- misc ----
#
# baseparameter was listed here too. It is a Rockchip partition read by their
# hwcomposer for the saved display mode; that HAL is gone, flash/partitions.tsv
# does not create the partition, and nothing left in the tree opens it.
/dev/block/by-name/misc      /misc      emmc  defaults  defaults

# ---- removable ----
#
# vold matches these patterns against the block device's sysfs path, so they have
# to name the nodes the *mainline* dts creates. Both were Rockchip BSP paths and
# neither could ever have matched:
#
#   fe320000.dwmmc -> fe320000.mmc. The SD controller is "sdmmc: mmc@fe320000" in
#     rk3399-base.dtsi, and a platform device is named <address>.<node name>. The
#     BSP called the node dwmmc@fe320000; mainline does not.
#   /devices/platform/usb* -> /devices/platform/*.usb*. Every USB controller on
#     this SoC is a "usb@<address>" node (fe380000, fe3a0000, fe3c0000, fe3e0000,
#     fe800000, fe900000), so nothing is ever called "usb" directly under
#     platform/. The address has to be allowed to come first.
#
# vold's match is fnmatch without FNM_PATHNAME, so * crosses / and one pattern
# covers the controller, the hub and the block device below it.
#
# No entry for the SD slot (fe320000.mmc) while Android boots FROM the card. vold
# would take the boot card for removable storage: it mounts any "basic data" GPT
# partition as a public volume, and bootfs is one (type 0700, so the eMMC's U-Boot
# finds it) - a second mount of the FAT that edge1-bootwatch writes logs to - and
# Settings would offer to format the card the system runs from. Once it runs from
# the eMMC, the slot is a real removable slot again and this line comes back:
#   /devices/platform/fe320000.mmc/mmc_host*  /storage/sdcard1  vfat  nosuid,nodev  wait,voldmanaged=sdcard1:auto
/devices/platform/*.usb*                        /storage/usbotg   vfat  nosuid,nodev  wait,voldmanaged=usbotg:auto
